    "number": 1958,
    "state": "open",
    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Document that the sha256 compression override sees secret keys",
    "body": "`secp256k1_context_set_sha256_compression` (include/secp256k1.h) does not say that the supplied function hashes secret data. It does: it hashes the secret key, or a value masked with it, when deriving RFC 6979, BIP340 and MuSig nonces, and the seed of the ecmult_gen blinding. A function that is not constant-time, or that logs or keeps its input, therefore breaks the library's constant-time and memory-clearing properties.\n\nCould the header say that the function processes secret keys and nonces, must run in constant time with respect to its input, and must not keep or log it? I can open the pull request if that wording suits you.\n\n*Assisted-by: my usual tools (LLM, Internet, computer). Mistakes are mine.*\n",
